    "created_at": "2021-05-12T10:41:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-12T10:41:29Z",
    "body": "Chrome and Safari seem to support it for type=range (although they don't render labels). E.g.,\r\n```html\r\n<input type=range list=x min=0 max=100>\r\n<datalist id=x><option value=23 label=Twenty-three></datalist>\r\n```\r\nWe could consider removal elsewhere I suppose, although it seems like it would be mainly a progressive enhancement so I don't really want to discourage implementers either.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
